column2:
1. Moderate pulmonary edema.
 2. Small bilateral pleural effusion.  Bibasilar atelectasis worse on the left;
 underlying infection cannot be excluded.

Transvenous right atrial ventricular pacer leads follow their expected courses
 from the left pectoral generator.  There is no pneumothorax, pleural effusion,
 or mediastinal widening.  Lungs are clear.

Bibasilar linear opacities, most suggestive of atelectasis;
 however, infection is not completely excluded, particularly at the left lung
 base.  Clinical correlation suggested.
